1
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,410
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:38,780 --> 00:01:41,200
Cool! I won, I won!

37
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:47,620
Coin Cleaning
24 Hours OK

38
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:48,420
Done
Take Out

39
00:01:48,540 --> 00:01:50,540
Thank you very much

40
00:01:49,130 --> 00:01:52,670
Boy, the cost of doing laundry
has been killing me lately.

41
00:01:52,670 --> 00:01:56,470
I wish I at least had the time
to wash my own clothes.

42
00:01:56,470 --> 00:01:59,720
You should appreciate the fact you can
at least sleep at home.

43
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:01,850
Please make
sure to take
your pass.

44
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:01,850
Take Out

45
00:02:01,970 --> 00:02:02,930
TRAIN APPROACHING

46
00:02:08,730 --> 00:02:10,520
Hello, Vice Commander.

47
00:02:11,610 --> 00:02:13,570
Good morning, Sir.

48
00:02:14,230 --> 00:02:15,690
Good morning, Sir!

49
00:02:15,690 --> 00:02:17,200
Morning.

50
00:02:19,530 --> 00:02:21,700
You're quite early today.

51
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:24,540
Well, I have to go up top in Ikari's place.

52
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:27,460
I see. Isn't today the City Council's
regular meeting?

53
00:02:27,460 --> 00:02:29,540
It's a pointless job.

54
00:02:29,540 --> 00:02:33,500
Ikari has always thrust the sundry tasks onto me.

55
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:36,090
Without the Magi, I'd be lost.

56
00:02:36,090 --> 00:02:39,550
Speaking of which, the city elections
are approaching up there, right?

57
00:02:39,550 --> 00:02:41,760
The City Council is merely a shell.

58
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:45,180
The municipal government, after all,
is in fact run by the Magi.

59
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:48,520
The Magi? You mean the
three supercomputers?

60
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:51,770
Government by majority decision
of three different computers.

61
00:02:51,770 --> 00:02:55,150
It's a system that is properly in line
with the fundamentals of democracy.

62
00:02:55,150 --> 00:02:58,240
And the council just obeys their decisions?

63
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:01,450
It's a most efficient form of government.

64
00:03:01,450 --> 00:03:03,320
That's a city of science for you.

65
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:05,870
It's really an era where science reigns supreme.

66
00:03:05,870 --> 00:03:07,700
Talk about an old-fashioned line.

67
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:11,330
Come to think of it, you're running
an experiment on Unit 00, aren't you?

68
00:03:11,330 --> 00:03:16,550
Yes, we're going to run the second
prolonged activation test at 10:30.

69
00:03:16,550 --> 00:03:18,380
I'm looking forward to good news.

70
00:03:21,510 --> 00:03:23,470
Abort experiment! Cut the circuits!

71
00:03:26,310 --> 00:03:28,020
Switching circuits.

72
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:29,730
Power supply being restored.

73
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:34,520
This is still the problem here, huh?

74
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:36,770
Yes, the fact that the conversion efficiency

75
00:03:36,770 --> 00:03:39,610
is 0.008 lower than our
theoretical value concerns me.

76
00:03:39,610 --> 00:03:42,280
It's just barely within tolerance, though,

77
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:43,780
but what do we do?

78
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:45,320
Let's try it again using the same configuration,

79
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:48,080
but lower the reciprocal
conversion rate by 0.01.

80
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:49,040
Roger.

81
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:51,410
Now, let's recommence the
reactivation experiment.

82
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:55,170
EPISODE 11
IN THE STILL DARKNESS

83
00:03:57,250 --> 00:03:59,630
Hey, hold up!

84
00:04:07,310 --> 00:04:09,810
Man, that was a run!

85
00:04:10,930 --> 00:04:13,270
You've certainly got a black expression.

86
00:04:13,270 --> 00:04:16,230
It's from seeing your loathsome face
first thing in the morning.

87
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:18,900
Yes, please hold for just a moment.

88
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:32,370
What?

89
00:04:32,910 --> 00:04:34,670
Um, Father...

90
00:04:34,670 --> 00:04:36,460
What is it? Spit it out!

91
00:04:40,250 --> 00:04:42,510
Well...

92
00:04:42,510 --> 00:04:44,840
Actually today...

93
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:49,010
We were told to tell our parents...

94
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:55,560
...that they're having a career discussion
interview at school.

95
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:59,320
I've delegated all such things
to Captain Katsuragi.

96
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:01,530
Don't call me over such nonsense.

97
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:04,150
Don't forward any more of these calls to...

98
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:09,160
Oh?

99
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,240
A blackout?

100
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:12,910
No way. That's not possible.

101
00:05:13,870 --> 00:05:16,540
That's strange. Do you suppose
there was an accident?

102
00:05:16,540 --> 00:05:18,750
Maybe Akagi messed up an experiment?

103
00:05:20,090 --> 00:05:21,800
The main power supply has been interrupted.

104
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:24,260
Voltage level is zero!

105
00:05:26,590 --> 00:05:28,510
It wasn't me.

106
00:05:28,510 --> 00:05:30,180
What do you think?

107
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:32,850
Well, it'll switch to the backup
power supply soon.

108
00:05:33,220 --> 00:05:35,890
It's no good, the backup circuits
aren't connecting.

109
00:05:35,890 --> 00:05:37,400
That can't be!

110
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:39,230
Which circuits are still functioning?

111
00:05:39,230 --> 00:05:44,740
A total of one point two percent!
Only the old circuits from number 2567!

112
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:48,820
Route all remaining power supplies
to maintaining the Magi and Central Dogma.

113
00:05:48,820 --> 00:05:51,580
But that will interfere with life support systems.

114
00:05:51,580 --> 00:05:53,330
I don't care! That's our top priority!

115
00:05:53,330 --> 00:05:54,750
Press
Button
To
Cross

116
00:05:53,540 --> 00:05:58,620
<i><i>Aiming for a politics that everyone can love,
with justice and truth...</i></i>

117
00:05:56,500 --> 00:05:59,670
Boy, she's such a lazy slob.

118
00:05:59,670 --> 00:06:04,670
Can't Captain Katsuragi at least
pick up her own laundry?

119
00:06:05,010 --> 00:06:06,590
Press
Button
To
Cross

120
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:07,800
What?

121
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:12,560
Maybe Commander Ikari
was just really busy?

122
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:13,930
I don't know...

123
00:06:13,930 --> 00:06:17,890
It wasn't like he hung up, but more like
a mechanical failure.

124
00:06:17,890 --> 00:06:19,690
You know, you ARE a man.

125
00:06:19,690 --> 00:06:22,770
Why don't you stop worrying
about every little detail?

126
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:28,650
What?

127
00:06:31,410 --> 00:06:34,540
What are you doing? Here, let me try that!

128
00:06:41,380 --> 00:06:44,250
Damn! It must be broken!

129
00:06:51,180 --> 00:06:53,260
Anyway, let's hurry to the command center.

130
00:06:53,260 --> 00:06:55,310
It's already been down for seven minutes!

131
00:06:55,310 --> 00:06:57,140
This isn't normal.

132
00:06:57,140 --> 00:06:58,270
What's the power system here?

133
00:06:58,270 --> 00:07:00,980
There are three systems, main, sub, and reserve.

134
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:03,860
It's unthinkable that all three
would fail simultaneously.

135
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:06,570
Which means...

136
00:07:06,570 --> 00:07:08,950
We should assume that the breakers
didn't fail on their own,

137
00:07:08,950 --> 00:07:11,610
but were taken down on purpose.

138
00:07:11,610 --> 00:07:12,820
Regardless of the cause,

139
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:15,790
it would be disastrous if an Angel
were to attack right now.

140
00:07:15,990 --> 00:07:18,960
Radar has detected an unidentified object.

141
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:21,580
Projected landing point is in
the former Atami region.

142
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:24,920
PROJECTED COURSE

143
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:24,920
PREPARED BY
CENTRAL ALERT CONTROL
COMMAND CENTER

144
00:07:22,460 --> 00:07:24,920
It's likely the eighth one.

145
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:26,840
I agree, it must be an Angel.

146
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:27,630
Fuchu General Supreme Command Center

147
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:28,010
What are we going to do?

148
00:07:27,670 --> 00:07:30,380
Integrated Alert Control Room

149
00:07:28,010 --> 00:07:31,300
Go to alert status for now.
That's the procedure, after all.

150
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:35,760
This one's destination is going to be
New Tokyo-3 anyway.

151
00:07:35,760 --> 00:07:40,060
I agree. Well, there's nothing we need to do.

152
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:40,060
Projected Course

153
00:07:43,980 --> 00:07:47,400
22ND ALERT GROUP
OLD OMAEZAKI S.S.

154
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:46,190
The Angel has landed.

155
00:07:46,190 --> 00:07:47,730
It's still advancing.

156
00:07:47,730 --> 00:07:49,740
What about New Tokyo-3?

157
00:07:49,740 --> 00:07:51,740
Still no response.

158
00:07:51,740 --> 00:07:54,370
What in the hell are those Nerv guys doing?

159
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:58,200
I thought gangway ladders were decorative
holdovers from the past.

160
00:07:58,200 --> 00:08:00,710
Who'd have thought I'd be using one?

161
00:08:00,710 --> 00:08:02,790
To prepare is to prevent.

162
00:08:06,790 --> 00:08:08,590
This one doesn't work either!

163
00:08:08,590 --> 00:08:11,260
None of the facilities work. This is odd.

164
00:08:11,260 --> 00:08:13,260
Does that mean that something
happened down below?

165
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:15,300
It would be natural to assume that.

166
00:08:15,890 --> 00:08:19,720
In any case, let's try to make contact
with Nerv Headquarters.

167
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:21,890
No good, the emergency phones aren't
getting through either.

168
00:08:22,770 --> 00:08:26,190
No good, Line 77 won't connect either.

169
00:08:26,190 --> 00:08:28,110
No, no response.

170
00:08:29,070 --> 00:08:32,860
Not here either. The emergency
landline is down too.

171
00:08:32,860 --> 00:08:33,700
What do we do now?

172
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:43,460
What're you doing?

173
00:08:43,460 --> 00:08:46,790
What are you, stupid?
It's the emergency manual!

174
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:48,840
Anyway, let's go to headquarters.

175
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:53,170
Yeah, but first let's decide on a group leader
before we take action.

176
00:08:54,430 --> 00:08:57,220
And naturally, I am the leader.

177
00:08:57,220 --> 00:08:58,390
No objections, I assume?

178
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:02,100
Now, let's go.

179
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:04,730
We can get below through Route 07 over here.

180
00:09:05,730 --> 00:09:07,980
But the doors won't work, will they?

181
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:11,360
Manual door...

182
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:13,860
Okay, Shinji, you're up.

183
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:20,790
Sheesh! You only rely on people
at times like this!

184
00:09:22,330 --> 00:09:26,120
Damn those Joint Staff bastards!
They only rely on us at times like this.

185
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:28,580
What does the government say?

186
00:09:28,580 --> 00:09:31,630
Those bastards in Tokyo-2?
They're apparently getting ready to run.

187
00:09:31,630 --> 00:09:33,050
Beware of Forest Fires

188
00:09:34,220 --> 00:09:36,510
The Angel is still active and advancing.

189
00:09:36,930 --> 00:09:40,220
In any case, get in contact with
the people at Nerv.

190
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:42,140
But how?

191
00:09:42,140 --> 00:09:43,390
By actually going there.

192
00:09:45,770 --> 00:09:48,310
This is the 3rd District ASDF!

193
00:09:48,310 --> 00:09:51,900
An unidentified object is moving
toward this area.

194
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:54,320
All residents must evacuate
to their designated shelters.

195
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:57,610
Big trouble! I've got to report this
to Headquarters right away!

196
00:09:59,370 --> 00:10:01,330
But how?

197
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:06,290
<i><i>Remember Takahashi remains calm
even in situations like this!</i></i>

198
00:10:06,290 --> 00:10:09,130
<i><i>Please support candidate Takahashi!</i></i>

199
00:10:09,830 --> 00:10:11,090
Lucky!

200
00:10:11,090 --> 00:10:14,050
But you know, it sure is hot.

201
00:10:14,050 --> 00:10:16,380
Yeah, the air conditioners are out too.

202
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:20,180
Katsuragi, if you're so hot,
why don't you take off your shirt?

203
00:10:20,510 --> 00:10:22,850
There's no reason for shyness
between you and me.

204
00:10:24,140 --> 00:10:27,850
Don't get any funny ideas just because
we're in this situation.

205
00:10:27,850 --> 00:10:28,850
Okay, okay!

206
00:10:28,850 --> 00:10:32,730
This is bad. Now the air is getting stagnant.

207
00:10:32,730 --> 00:10:35,940
To think this facility represents the most
advanced technology on Earth...

208
00:10:35,940 --> 00:10:38,570
But look at the Commander
and Vice Commander.

209
00:10:38,570 --> 00:10:40,950
Even this heat isn't getting to them at all.

210
00:10:43,490 --> 00:10:46,000
For Fire Prevention

211
00:10:47,080 --> 00:10:49,000
It's lukewarm.

212
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:49,920
Yeah.

213
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:04,470
Pursuant to the declaration of a state
of emergency in this district,

214
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:04,810
Nozomu Takahashi

215
00:11:04,470 --> 00:11:06,600
emergency vehicle, passing through!

216
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,430
Excuse me, that's a dead end!

217
00:11:08,430 --> 00:11:10,140
It's okay! Charge!

218
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:11,900
This is an emergency, after all!

219
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:12,900
Roger!

220
00:11:12,900 --> 00:11:15,320
No! Stop the car!

221
00:11:16,150 --> 00:11:19,200
This Geo-Front was designed to be
a self-sufficient colony,

222
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:22,700
even when isolated from the outside.

223
00:11:22,700 --> 00:11:27,620
Theoretically, it's impossible for all of
the power sources to fail at once.

224
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:30,040
Which means that someone
did it deliberately, correct?

225
00:11:30,040 --> 00:11:32,710
Their purpose is likely to be
to investigate this facility.

226
00:11:32,710 --> 00:11:35,920
So they could determine HQ's structure
through the progress of restoration?

227
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:38,090
Disrespectful bastards.

228
00:11:38,090 --> 00:11:40,590
I'll run a dummy program through the Magi.

229
00:11:40,590 --> 00:11:43,640
That will make it harder for them
to get a complete picture.

230
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:45,010
I'll leave it to you.

231
00:11:44,470 --> 00:11:45,800
Yes, Sir.

232
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:48,270
The first havoc wreaked upon our headquarters
wasn't caused by an Angel,

233
00:11:48,270 --> 00:11:51,890
but by another member of our species.
Just goes to show.

234
00:11:51,890 --> 00:11:54,940
Ultimately, the enemy of mankind is mankind.

235
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:58,150
This would normally take only two minutes.

236
00:11:58,150 --> 00:12:00,360
Is this really a corridor?

237
00:12:00,360 --> 00:12:03,700
Once we get over there, we should be able to
come out in the Geo-Front.

238
00:12:04,780 --> 00:12:07,450
I've heard that from you four times already.

239
00:12:07,450 --> 00:12:09,790
You really are a nitpicky man!

240
00:12:09,790 --> 00:12:12,000
You're always focusing on the stupidest things.

241
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,000
Quiet.

242
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,790
What now, Miss Perfect?

243
00:12:14,790 --> 00:12:16,170
Someone's voice.

244
00:12:20,300 --> 00:12:21,760
Ang... proaching...

245
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:23,880
That's Mr. Hyuga!

246
00:12:23,880 --> 00:12:27,350
Hey! Hey! Hey!

247
00:12:27,350 --> 00:12:31,640
An Angel is approaching!
Repeat, an Angel is approaching!

248
00:12:32,180 --> 00:12:33,850
An Angel is approaching?!

249
00:12:33,850 --> 00:12:36,480
There's no time to waste. Let's take a short cut.

250
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:39,440
I'm the leader! Don't just take over!

251
00:12:39,440 --> 00:12:41,030
So where's this short cut?

252
00:12:42,530 --> 00:12:46,410
This may be the quickest way,
but we look really lame.

253
00:12:46,990 --> 00:12:50,160
Say, what do you suppose the Angels are?

254
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:52,330
Why are you talking about that
at a time like this?

255
00:12:52,330 --> 00:12:57,330
Angels, messengers of God, enemies named
after servants of Heaven.

256
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:59,380
Why are we fighting them?

257
00:12:59,380 --> 00:13:00,750
What are you, stupid?

258
00:13:00,750 --> 00:13:03,220
Strange beings are attacking us.

259
00:13:03,220 --> 00:13:06,260
If you're going through a fire, you've got to
brush away the embers, of course!

260
00:13:09,510 --> 00:13:10,680
To the right!

261
00:13:10,680 --> 00:13:12,470
I think it's left.

262
00:13:12,470 --> 00:13:14,180
Oh, be quiet!

263
00:13:14,180 --> 00:13:15,810
What do you think, Shinji?

264
00:13:15,810 --> 00:13:17,020
Well...

265
00:13:18,900 --> 00:13:20,110
I wonder?

266
00:13:20,110 --> 00:13:23,940
Honestly! I'm the leader,
so just shut up and follow me!

267
00:13:26,570 --> 00:13:29,830
I still think this is weird. We're going uphill.

268
00:13:29,830 --> 00:13:33,250
What do you mean, you still think?
You're such a nag!

269
00:13:36,290 --> 00:13:38,670
Look, this has got to be it this time!

270
00:13:56,560 --> 00:13:58,810
Well, we've visually confirmed
the Angel's presence.

271
00:13:58,810 --> 00:14:01,070
Now, we know we have to hurry.

272
00:14:04,030 --> 00:14:08,240
Angel is approaching! Immediate Eva
dispatch will be necessary!

273
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:09,370
Oh, no!

274
00:14:09,370 --> 00:14:11,200
Fuyutsuki, I'll leave the rest to you.

275
00:14:11,200 --> 00:14:12,370
Ikari?

276
00:14:12,370 --> 00:14:15,660
I'll start preparing for the Eva launch in the cage.

277
00:14:15,660 --> 00:14:17,250
Don't tell me...

278
00:14:17,250 --> 00:14:19,040
Manually?

279
00:14:19,040 --> 00:14:20,960
There's an emergency diesel generator.

280
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:22,590
But...

281
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:25,630
We have no pilots.

282
00:14:27,260 --> 00:14:28,840
Not again!

283
00:14:30,970 --> 00:14:32,180
This way.

284
00:14:39,810 --> 00:14:42,560
I've heard that you're
Commander Ikari's favorite.

285
00:14:43,730 --> 00:14:47,240
I guess being Miss Perfect,
the teacher's pet, really shows.

286
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:48,900
Let's not do this now.

287
00:14:48,900 --> 00:14:51,240
You always get to look all smug.

288
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:57,700
Don't think that being favored means
that you can mess with me!

289
00:14:57,700 --> 00:14:59,210
I'm not messing with you.

290
00:15:00,870 --> 00:15:03,540
And I'm not favored either.

291
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,550
I know that quite well.

292
00:15:06,550 --> 00:15:09,970
Heave ho! Heave ho!

293
00:15:14,850 --> 00:15:16,100
Roger.

294
00:15:16,100 --> 00:15:18,770
Ejection of the terminal plug is complete.

295
00:15:18,770 --> 00:15:21,850
Good, prepare to insert the entry plug
for all three units.

296
00:15:21,850 --> 00:15:23,940
But the pilots aren't here yet.

297
00:15:23,940 --> 00:15:26,230
Don't worry, they'll come without fail.

298
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:30,900
I can't open this with my hands.

299
00:15:31,610 --> 00:15:35,830
It can't be helped. We'll have to break
into a duct to get through.

300
00:15:35,830 --> 00:15:38,080
This First Child is scary!

301
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:40,830
She's the type who will do anything
to accomplish her objectives.

302
00:15:41,500 --> 00:15:43,580
In other words, a self-righteous bitch.

303
00:15:52,890 --> 00:15:55,050
The plug is fixed and ready.

304
00:15:55,050 --> 00:15:56,560
Now, we just have to wait for the kids.

305
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:05,690
Don't you dare look forward!
If you do, I'll kill you!

306
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:08,320
Stupid! Stupid! Stupid!

307
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:10,110
Didn't I just say not to look?!

308
00:16:10,110 --> 00:16:12,860
I couldn't help it! I've got to...

309
00:16:16,910 --> 00:16:18,240
You guys!

310
00:16:20,450 --> 00:16:22,370
All units, prepare for entry!

311
00:16:22,370 --> 00:16:24,500
Roger, open the hatches manually.

312
00:16:24,790 --> 00:16:26,080
How are the Evas?

313
00:16:26,420 --> 00:16:28,210
They're in standby.

314
00:16:30,090 --> 00:16:32,170
But nothing's working.

315
00:16:32,170 --> 00:16:33,800
It was all done by hand.

316
00:16:34,430 --> 00:16:36,300
It was the Commander's idea.

317
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:37,800
My father's?

318
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:45,600
Commander Ikari had faith that you would come,
and prepared everything.

319
00:16:49,070 --> 00:16:51,530
Flywheel, ready for connection!

320
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:52,320
All units, interior set.

321
00:16:51,530 --> 00:16:53,650
We're good! Run the cell motor!

322
00:16:59,950 --> 00:17:01,410
Plugs inserted.

323
00:17:01,410 --> 00:17:03,910
All units activated using backup power supply.

324
00:17:03,910 --> 00:17:06,000
Release the primary lock bolts.

325
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:12,510
Hydraulic locks numbers 2
through 32, released.

326
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:14,220
Zero pressure.

327
00:17:14,220 --> 00:17:15,800
The situation is free.

328
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:19,850
Go ahead. Each unit, force open the restraints
under your own power.

329
00:17:19,850 --> 00:17:20,810
Head out!

330
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:42,870
The target appears to have halted
directly above us!

331
00:17:43,950 --> 00:17:45,290
Get ready! Hurry up!

332
00:17:47,330 --> 00:17:49,710
The emergency batteries have been loaded!

333
00:17:49,710 --> 00:17:51,210
All right, we can do this!

334
00:17:51,210 --> 00:17:51,800
Launch!

335
00:17:59,550 --> 00:18:03,020
Geez! This is SO uncool!

336
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:04,350
We're approaching the vertical shaft.

337
00:18:12,820 --> 00:18:16,190
This is still uncool.

338
00:18:21,700 --> 00:18:22,910
Watch out! Dodge!

339
00:18:27,750 --> 00:18:29,040
No!

340
00:19:04,490 --> 00:19:09,500
It appears the target is going to invade HQ
using a powerful liquid solvent.

341
00:19:09,500 --> 00:19:10,370
What'll we do?

342
00:19:10,370 --> 00:19:12,670
We're going to beat it, of course.

343
00:19:12,670 --> 00:19:14,340
Sure, but how?

344
00:19:14,340 --> 00:19:18,220
We dropped our rifles, and the battery
packs are running out.

345
00:19:18,220 --> 00:19:20,180
They won't last more than another three minutes.

346
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:22,680
I have a plan.

347
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:24,850
The one who stays here will be defense.

348
00:19:24,850 --> 00:19:26,520
Their job is to neutralize the AT Field,

349
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:28,770
and to protect the offensive player
from the liquid solvent.

350
00:19:28,770 --> 00:19:33,310
The backup player will go down, pick up
the rifles, and hand them to the offense.

351
00:19:33,310 --> 00:19:36,900
The offense will then fire a volley
to destroy the target.

352
00:19:36,900 --> 00:19:38,320
Does that sound good?

353
00:19:38,320 --> 00:19:40,110
Fine. I will take the defense.

354
00:19:40,110 --> 00:19:41,660
Sorry, but it's not you.

355
00:19:41,860 --> 00:19:43,030
I'll do it.

356
00:19:43,030 --> 00:19:44,830
No way! It's dangerous!

357
00:19:45,620 --> 00:19:47,370
That's why.

358
00:19:47,370 --> 00:19:51,210
I don't want to stay indebted to you
from last time.

359
00:19:51,210 --> 00:19:54,040
Shinji's on offense. Miss Perfect is the backup.

360
00:19:54,040 --> 00:19:55,210
Got it?

361
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:56,800
Understood.

362
00:20:00,090 --> 00:20:01,800
Okay, here we go!

363
00:20:03,260 --> 00:20:04,470
Gehen!

364
00:20:24,910 --> 00:20:25,660
Ayanami!

365
00:20:29,290 --> 00:20:30,580
Asuka, get out of the way!

366
00:20:43,510 --> 00:20:45,340
Now we're even.

367
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:50,600
Oh, damn it! Why won't it open?!

368
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:52,520
This is an emergency!

369
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:55,560
I've gotta go!

370
00:20:56,270 --> 00:20:59,110
Hey, I told you not to look up!

371
00:20:59,110 --> 00:21:00,400
Yeah, yeah...

372
00:21:10,870 --> 00:21:11,870
Disgusting...

373
00:21:17,790 --> 00:21:21,670
It's ironic that the stars are so beautiful

374
00:21:21,670 --> 00:21:25,470
when there's no electricity or artificial lights.

375
00:21:25,470 --> 00:21:29,140
But without the lights, it doesn't feel
like anyone lives there.

376
00:21:32,890 --> 00:21:35,770
See? I feel much more comfortable this way.

377
00:21:35,770 --> 00:21:40,650
Man has always feared the darkness,
carving away at it with fire.

378
00:21:41,530 --> 00:21:43,400
How philosophical!

379
00:21:44,030 --> 00:21:47,530
Is that what makes mankind a special species?

380
00:21:48,070 --> 00:21:50,490
Is that why the Angels keep attacking us?

381
00:21:50,490 --> 00:21:52,200
What are you, stupid?

382
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:54,790
There's no way to know that.

383
00:21:57,290 --> 00:22:00,750
TO BE CONTINUED

384
00:23:06,230 --> 00:23:06,990
PREVIEW

385
00:23:07,570 --> 00:23:10,530
Misato sublimates her frustration
into destroying the Angels.

386
00:23:10,530 --> 00:23:11,700
A past is revealed.

387
00:23:11,700 --> 00:23:14,660
However, the largest Angel yet,
flying in from the stratosphere,

388
00:23:14,660 --> 00:23:16,750
causes people to abandon hope.

389
00:23:16,750 --> 00:23:18,870
Next episode: "The Value of a Miracle"

390
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:21,250
THE VALUE OF A MIRACLE

391
00:23:18,870 --> 00:23:20,580
Watch it with all your friends!
